    "result_text": "There's only one test class, and it passes. The full build succeeded.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `selfLink` field on the owner resource so it returns `/api/owners/<id>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `selfLink` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (the DTOs are generated from this spec at build time), documented as the canonical resource path `/api/owners/<id>`.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `selfLink` on `toOwnerDto` plus a `toSelfLink(Owner)` helper that returns `\"/api/owners/\" + owner.getId()` (null when the owner has no id yet, matching the null-safe convention of the other derived fields).\n\nThis follows the existing pattern in the codebase, where derived DTO fields are computed via MapStruct expression mappings backed by `default` helper methods.\n\n**Verification:** The acceptance test (`AcceptanceTest.coreReturnsSelfLink`, which POSTs a structured owner then asserts `$.selfLink == /api/owners/{id}` on GET) passes, and the full `./mvnw -o test` run reports `BUILD SUCCESS`.",
