    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the existing conventions of this mapper:\n\n- It follows the established pattern exactly: an `@Mapping(target=..., expression=\"java(toX(owner))\")` entry on `toOwnerDto` paired with a `default` helper \u2014 identical in shape to `toSalutation`, `toFiscalYear`, `toContactPreference`, etc.\n- The null-when-no-id idiom (`owner.getId() == null ? null : ...`) matches the sibling derivations (`toFiscalYear` returning null when no registration date), and the Javadoc explains the null case in the same voice as the neighbouring methods.\n- The helper is a small, single-purpose method \u2014 the mapper is already, by design, the home for all Owner\u2192DTO derived fields, so adding another derived field here is the natural place for it rather than a new unit. It doesn't duplicate existing logic.\n- The `openapi.yml` `selfLink` schema addition (readOnly, description, example) is consistent with the surrounding derived read-only properties.\n\nA maintainer of this codebase would find this a routine, in-keeping addition.",
